{
  "Version": 2,
  "Name": "Matuschek1998-DCM-quadratic-match",
  "Source": "N. Matuschek, F. X. Kärtner, and U. Keller, \"Theory of double-chirped mirrors,\" IEEE J. Sel. Top. Quantum Electron. 4, 197-208 (1998). doi:10.1109/2944.686723 - Sec. IV-C text p. 203-204, Fig. 7(b) solid curve; Fig. 2 solid curve",
  "Notes": "Double-chirped mirror with quadratically chirped (alpha = 2) high-index thickness over the first 12 steps (Z(0) = 1 and Z'(0) = 0)\nSpecification: Very smooth group delay over the high-reflectivity range\nReported: Very smooth group delay at the expense of part of the high-reflectivity range (Fig. 7(b)); high reflectivity roughly 620-1000 nm from the plot. Sec. V approximate expressions (for a linearly chirped mirror with kappa0 = -0.5, k0 = 10.47 um^-1, k1 = 0.17 um^-1): GDD ~ -52 fs^2 and TOD ~ 21 fs^3 at 800 nm (k/k0 = 0.75) - analytic estimates, not exact.\nNotes: Construction (Sec. IV-C, Figs. 3, 6, 7): 25 symmetric index steps, each = 1/2 d_l | d_h | 1/2 d_l (Fig. 3), n_h = 2.5, n_l = 1.5, no dispersion. Bragg wavelength of step |m| (|m| = 1 at the front, where light enters): k_B = k0 - (|m|-1)(k0 - kmin)/19 for |m| = 1..20 with k0 = 2pi/600 nm, kmin = 2pi/900 nm; |m| = 21..25 kept at kmin. Bragg wavelength = 2 (n_h d_h + n_l d_l). The paper computes reflectivity with respect to the first low-index (SiO2-like) layer and explicitly ignores the jump to air, so the incident medium is taken as n = 1.5 (the front half-low layer merges into it); the back half-low layer merges into the n = 1.5 (SiO2) substrate. Adjacent half low layers of steps m and m+1 are merged, giving 49 layers (25 H, 24 L). Thicknesses computed by me from the stated formulas (rounded to 0.001 nm); layer 1 = front (incident side), last H layer is next to the substrate. For |m| <= 12, d_h = (lambda_B(12)/(4 n_h)) (|m|/12)^2; for |m| > 12 quarter-wave; d_l = (lambda_B/2 - n_h d_h)/n_l. Note the paper quotes k1 = 0.17 um^-1 although (k0 - kmin)/19 = 0.184 um^-1 per step; the Sec. V numbers are approximations only.\nLayers from Sec. IV-C text p. 203-204, Fig. 7(b) solid curve; Fig. 2 solid curve; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nNot checked: the paper reports this design only as plots.",
